---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastReviewed = '2026-05-05';
const siteOrigin = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_URL || 'https://defycard.com';
const breadcrumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', url: `${siteOrigin}/` },
  { name: 'Terms of use', url: `${siteOrigin}/terms/` },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use — DefyCard"
  description="DefyCard terms of use: informational only, affiliate-link consent, intellectual property, acceptable use, jurisdiction, and limitation of liability."
  activeNav="cards"
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
>
  <article class="legal-page">
    <h1>Terms of use</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      These terms govern your use of <a href="https://defycard.com">defycard.com</a>
      and any subdomain operated by DefyCard. By loading any page on this
      site you agree to the terms below. If you do not agree, please leave
      the site.
    </p>

    <h2>Informational purposes only</h2>
    <p>
      Every article, comparison, calculator, and review on DefyCard is
      published for informational purposes. Nothing on this site constitutes
      investment advice, financial advice, tax advice, legal advice, or a
      recommendation to buy, sell, or hold any digital asset. DefyCard is
      not a registered investment adviser, broker-dealer, securities
      exchange, money-services business, or Crypto Asset Service Provider.
      Decisions you make about a crypto card, an issuer, or any digital
      asset are your own. You should consult a qualified professional
      before acting on any information you find here.
    </p>

    <h2>Capital at risk</h2>
    <p>
      Crypto debit and credit cards depend on underlying crypto assets, on
      issuer custody arrangements, and on third-party settlement networks.
      Each of those layers carries operational, regulatory, and market risk.
      Cashback yields, FX fees, country availability, and KYC requirements
      can change at any time without notice. Past performance does not
      indicate future results, and a card that fits your needs today may
      not fit them in twelve months.
    </p>

    <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>
      DefyCard contains affiliate links. By clicking such a link you
      acknowledge that DefyCard may earn a commission from the destination
      issuer if you sign up. Commission does not change the price, terms,
      or cashback you receive. The
      <a href="/disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> page describes the
      mechanics in full.
    </p>

    <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      All editorial content (articles, structure, copy, scoring rubric,
      methodology) on DefyCard is owned by DefyCard or licensed to it. You
      may quote short excerpts (up to 100 words) for non-commercial use
      with attribution and a link back to the source page; broader
      reproduction, syndication, or republication requires written
      permission. Hero and inline images are licensed via Unsplash subject
      to the Unsplash License; photographer credits remain with the image.
    </p>

    <h2>Trademarks</h2>
    <p>
      DefyCard and the DefyCard logo are trademarks of DefyCard. References
      to ether.fi, Crypto.com, RedotPay, Bybit, MetaMask, Gnosis Pay,
      Coinbase, and other named issuers, networks, or wallets are made for
      identification purposes only and do not imply endorsement by, or
      affiliation with, those parties.
    </p>

    <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      You agree not to scrape, mirror, or republish the site at scale; not
      to attempt to bypass security controls, rate limits, or bot
      detection; not to use the site for any unlawful purpose; and not to
      probe or test the vulnerability of any DefyCard system without prior
      written permission. AI agents and crawlers are welcome subject to the
      directives in <code>/robots.txt</code> and the AI-readiness
      conventions documented at <code>/llms.txt</code> and
      <code>/.well-known/agent-skills/index.json</code>.
    </p>

    <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      DefyCard is provided “as is” and “as available.” To the fullest extent
      permitted by law, DefyCard, its operators, and its contributors
      disclaim all warranties, whether express or implied, including
      warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose,
      non-infringement, and availability. In no event will DefyCard be
      liable for any indirect, incidental, consequential, or punitive
      damages arising out of or in connection with your use of the site,
      even if advised of the possibility of such damages. Where applicable
      law does not permit such limitations, they apply to the maximum
      extent allowed.
    </p>

    <h2>Third-party content</h2>
    <p>
      DefyCard links to third-party websites, including card issuers, news
      outlets, and regulators. We are not responsible for the content,
      accuracy, or availability of those sites; an external link is not an
      endorsement of any opinion, product, or service hosted there.
    </p>

    <h2>Jurisdiction</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the operator’s domicile,
      without regard to conflict-of-law principles. Disputes arising out of
      or relating to these terms or your use of the site are subject to
      the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts in that domicile, except
      where local consumer-protection law grants you a non-waivable right
      to bring suit in your country of residence.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may revise these terms. Material revisions will update the “Last
      reviewed” date at the bottom of this page. Continued use of the site
      after a revision constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms?
      <a href="mailto:support@defycard.com">support@defycard.com</a>.
    </p>

    <p class="page-meta">Last reviewed: {lastReviewed}</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    max-width: 720px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .legal-page h2 {
    margin-top: 1.8em;
  }
  .legal-page p {
    color: var(--on-surface);
    margin: 0 0 1em;
  }
  .legal-page code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--surface-container-low);
    padding: 2px 6px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
  }
  .page-meta {
    margin-top: 48px;
    padding-top: 16px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--outline-variant);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--on-surface-variant);
  }
</style>
